Package: gmxdcc
Type: Package
Title: GARCH-MIDAS and DCC-MIDAS Models with Exogenous Covariates and
    Structural Breaks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("JIANCHANG", "LYU", email = "rokenshotlib124@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Two-step quasi-maximum-likelihood estimation of GARCH-MIDAS
    volatility models and cDCC, aDCC, DECO and DCC-MIDAS correlation
    models. The long-run components admit an arbitrary list of
    low-frequency covariates (including automatically generated realized
    volatility and realized correlation), each with its own MIDAS lag
    order, and piecewise-constant structural breaks in the long-run
    intercepts and slopes. Robust Bollerslev-Wooldridge (1992)
    <doi:10.1080/07474939208800229> sandwich standard errors are reported
    in both estimation steps. Likelihood recursions are implemented in
    C++ via 'Rcpp' and 'RcppArmadillo'.
